{
  "title": "Meta Lead Form → GoHighLevel Speed to Lead",
  "platform": "gohighlevel",
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "arrive",
      "label": "1 · THE LEAD ARRIVES",
      "color": 0,
      "note": "Meta posts straight into GoHighLevel rather than sitting in Ads Manager waiting to be pulled. The contact is matched on phone first so a repeat enquiry does not become a second record, then removed from any sequence already running on them. That removal step is what stops a lead getting two different messages from you in the same minute."
    },
    {
      "key": "speed",
      "label": "2 · FIRST 60 SECONDS",
      "color": 0,
      "note": "The text goes out before anyone has looked at the lead, and the rep's phone rings at the same time. Response time is the single biggest lever on lead-to-appointment rate, and it is the one thing that cannot be fixed later in the sequence."
    },
    {
      "key": "chase",
      "label": "3 · IF THEY GO QUIET",
      "color": 0,
      "note": "Spaced follow-up over the first day and a half, not a burst. Each touch is a different channel so the lead is not receiving three of the same message, and the sequence has a defined end rather than running forever."
    },
    {
      "key": "reply",
      "label": "4 · THE MOMENT THEY REPLY",
      "color": 0,
      "note": "Everything queued stops on the first reply, on any channel. The pipeline stage moves and the rep is told who replied and what they said, so nobody opens a conversation cold."
    },
    {
      "key": "track",
      "label": "5 · SO YOU CAN SEE IT WORKING",
      "color": 0,
      "note": "Response time is stamped on every lead, which turns speed to lead from a claim into a number you can open on a Monday and check per rep and per campaign."
    }
  ],
